Web Crawling

The process by which a search engine finds and fetches new or updated web pages is called crawling. To do so, they use automated programs called crawlers. Now, let us start with the first step to the crawling process, ‘URL Discovery’. The most common way for a crawler to discover new webpages or URLs is for it to traverse from a known page to a new one. The next and final step to the crawling process is fetching, where the crawler downloads all the data under a discovered URL. On a side note, XML sitemaps can also improve a website's discoverability under a web crawler. 

