Indexing

The next step after crawling is indexing. Indexing is the process by which the search engine understands what the web page is about. Indexing includes processing and analysing the textual content, key content tags, attributes, images and videos that the search engine will later use to rank the pages in its search results. Next, a search engine will parse through the html code and fix any errors (removal of unsupported tags). Next, the search engine checks if there are any duplicates of said webpage. Lastly, depending on the quality of the web page, it may or may not be chosen to be a part of the search engine’s database, this process is called index selection. 

